cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Please cite the preprint and its replay supplement. The manuscript text is licensed under CC-BY-4.0; the replay scripts and the remaining files are licensed under Apache-2.0.
title: 'Replay supplement for Worldline-cluster, annealed-spectral, and telescoping obstructions to a phonon-frequency pairing ceiling in the Holstein model'
authors:
- family-names: Rens
  given-names: Davis
  affiliation: SuperMatics Inc.
  orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5839-5197'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24425679
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  The tagged release tree of the preprint "Worldline-cluster, annealed-spectral, and
  telescoping obstructions to a phonon-frequency pairing ceiling in the Holstein model":
  the reviewed manuscript source, the released PDF and five standalone replay scripts that
  check every finite-arithmetic witness in exact rational and outward-interval arithmetic,
  with guarded mutant suites and a combined driver. The paper records what can be proved on
  both sides of the remaining gap toward a phonon-frequency pairing ceiling in the full Gibbs
  state of the spinful Holstein model, and where the worldline, telescoping, annealed-spectral,
  annealed-endpoint and neutral-dipole closure strategies break down at the specified
  constants. No pairing ceiling and no bound on any critical temperature is proved or
  disproved.
